    "one well per compound: well/field appearance is confounded with chemistry",
    "absolute scores are inflated for every method; the comparison against baseline_raw_pixels is what is interpretable",
    "one concentration per compound, so no dose-response is possible",
    "O2-VAE consumes a nucleus silhouette, not 5-channel intensity",
    "O2-VAE's official checkpoint was trained on CELL silhouettes (configs/config_mefs.py:19 -> data/mefs/scaled/cell) and no nucleus checkpoint is published, so feeding it a nucleus silhouette is OUT-OF-DOMAIN inference: the embedding distribution does not match the training distribution, and the number should not be read as the method's performance",
    "mock AUC is cross-validated over the 4 mock wells to avoid centroid self-inclusion bias",
    "rows marked SURROGATE use locally trained stand-in weights, not the authors'; their scores are an interface check, never a method result"
